# Generated parquet datasets — not checked in.
# Anchored to this dir (leading /) so they ONLY match the data dirs at
# testdata/<dataset>.sf<N>/ and NOT the committed goldens under
# testdata/goldens/<dataset>.sf<N>/ (the unanchored form caught those too).
/tpch.sf*/
/tpcds.sf*/

# Calibration output: the derived text is committed so `git diff` shows the numbers move
# (llm-wiki names each file's writer). The record is not: it lives in the `calibration`
# bucket keyed by its sha256, and records.sha256 pins the one this tree goes with. Ignored too: the nsys exports, hundreds of megabytes git cannot diff, and the
# counters pass's own record, whose microseconds are a profiler's.
# Deny-by-default, so a new file here is ignored until someone says otherwise. plots/ is
# re-included as two lines: git re-includes a directory happily, but its documented rule says
# a file under an excluded parent cannot be, and third-party matchers grey out plots/.
/calibration/*
!/calibration/records.sha256
!/calibration/hbm.tsv
!/calibration/calls.tsv
!/calibration/plots/
!/calibration/plots/**

# The device's recorded answers from a cuDF other than shad-gpu's 25.02. `gpu-result.txt`
# IS committed — one version per file, so the comparison with DuckDB reads one engine's
# answers — and a verify run writes `gpu-result-<version>.txt` beside it instead.
/goldens/*/gpu-result-*.txt
